#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""powos app - make, build, install and hot-reload PowOS apps (docs/POWOS-APPS-FEASIBILITY.md section 5).

An app is a directory: powos-app.json (the manifest), module/ (Rust -> a SpacetimeDB module: the app's state and
logic, in the device's own SpacetimeDB) and ui/ (Preact TSX the shell renders: a full-screen page in ui/pages/, home
widgets in ui/widgets/). No process of its own (Tier 0). An app with a page is an app in the launcher: the drawer,
search and the recent apps open it full screen; its widgets go on home from the edit sheet ("PowOS apps").

Make one (the whole loop, from a sentence to the phone - each step is one command):
  powos app new <name|id> [--name "Shown name"] [--template T] [--dir D]
                                     scaffold D (default ~/Projects/<name>): powos-app.json, module/src/lib.rs,
                                     ui/lib/app.ts, ui/pages/main.tsx, ui/widgets/main.tsx, ui/icon.svg.
                                     T: spacetimedb-astro (default: module + page + widget), widget (module +
                                     widget, no page), module-only (module, no UI). <name> without a dot gets the
                                     id local.<name>; the database is the id with dashes.
  powos app build <dir> [--local|--remote [user@host]] [--module|--ui]
                                     module -> out/module.wasm (+ TS bindings in ui/bindings), ui -> out/ui (bun).
                                     The module (Rust -> wasm) builds on the app builder (powos app builder) over
                                     ssh when one is set, else here if cargo + wasm32 are installed; the UI always
                                     builds here (bun, ~0.1 s). An unchanged module isn't rebuilt.
  powos app install <dir>            build (what changed), publish the module (unless the device's live module is this
                                     very build - checked against the database, not the local build), put the UI
                                     in place, register it
  powos app dev <dir>                hot reload while you edit: every save rebuilds what changed and pushes it -
                                     ui/ -> the open page and the widgets update in place (no restart, the data
                                     and the connection kept); module/ -> republished (schema kept, additive changes
                                     migrate), clients stay connected. Prints each step's time. Ctrl-C stops.
  powos app builder [user@host|local|off]
                                     where modules cross-compile: an ssh host with docker (or cargo + wasm32),
                                     e.g. the hub; the phone sends the module's source and gets the wasm back, so
                                     Rust never builds on its battery. Shown without an argument.

Change one:
  powos app publish <dir>            only the module again (rebuilt first if it changed): a hot swap, clients stay
                                     connected (logic hot reload)
  powos app ui <dir>                 only the UI again (rebuilt first; a new dir, `current` flipped atomically): the
                                     shell hot-reloads it
  powos app preview <dir|file.owl|widget-id> [--live] [--out D]
                                     every widget of it at every size it allows (minSize to 4x4), on the phone's
                                     cover and inner screens, in two themes, against mock data (shell/dev/preview/
                                     data/<id>.json): one contact sheet per widget, and the fit checks (clipped text,
                                     a row cut in half, a side >12% empty, content <25% of the tile, scrolling, a
                                     slider in a sideways scroller, hard borders). Exit 1 on a problem, each with its
                                     size. Runs shell/dev/preview.sh - where docker is (the Mac, a PowStation), from a
                                     PowOS checkout (POWOS_PREVIEW=<its preview.sh> elsewhere). A widget id is an OWL
                                     file's name (10-today), an app's widget (local.lights.main) or a panel (panel.agents).
  --note "..."                       on install/publish/ui: what changed, in plain words - the phone's quiet
                                     "update applied" notification (default: "<Name> app installed/updated")
  powos app list                     installed apps and widgets (from the registry)
  powos app remove <id> [--data]     unregister it and remove its files (its database stays; --data drops it too)

Writing one (what to edit after `new`):
  module/src/lib.rs   tables (#[spacetimedb::table(accessor = x, public)]) and reducers (#[spacetimedb::reducer]).
                      Keep schema changes additive: new tables, new columns at the END with #[default(..)];
                      a renamed/removed column is refused (then: new database name in powos-app.json).
  ui/pages/main.tsx   the full-screen page: export default function ({ host, close }) - app.useTable("x"),
                      app.useReducer("y") from ui/lib/app.ts. Reducer args are an object: add({ text }); u64 is
                      a bigint; snake_case fields arrive camelCase.
  ui/widgets/*.tsx    a home widget each (list it in powos-app.json "widgets"): ({ host, app, cells }). Make it
                      USABLE IN PLACE, not a preview: its actions inline (tick, -/+, remove), an add field, and
                      the header opening the page (host.openApp(app)); controls stop pointerdown propagating.
  The network:         "net": ["lan", "host.example"] in powos-app.json: what the app may reach ("lan" = any private
                      address). host.net.fetch(app, url, {method, headers, body}), host.net.useEvents(app, url,
                      headers, onEvent) (server-sent events, only while shown), host.net.mdns(app, "_x._tcp").
                      No CORS; a LAN device's self-signed certificate is pinned on first use. Keys stay in the
                      PowOS app: {capture: {secret: "k", path: "0.success.username"}} keeps one from a response,
                      "${secret:k}" in a header sends it. Example: ~/Projects/lights (Philips Hue).
  Styling: inline styles with the shell's theme variables (var(--color-accent), var(--color-foreground), ...).
  Imports: preact, preact/hooks, @preact/signals and spacetimedb come from the shell; anything else is bundled.

The system side:
  powos app runtime [<id> [<mode>]]  how an app's process runs: native | sandbox | container (powos-runtime)
  powos app services                 the system tier (powos-supervisor status)
  powos app check                    what this machine's runtimes can do (powos-runtime check)

Installed apps live in ~/.local/share/powos/apps/<id>/<version>/ with a `current` link; on the phone that directory
is the PowOS app's own files/apps (bound by rooted/powos-session.sh), which the shell serves at
https://shell.powos/_app/<id>/ and watches (a change there is the hot reload).
"""
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tarfile
import tempfile
import time

SERVER = os.environ.get("POWOS_STDB", "http://127.0.0.1:3410")
REGISTRY = "powos-registry"
REGISTRY_WASM = os.environ.get("POWOS_REGISTRY_WASM", "/usr/lib/powos/apps/registry/module.wasm")
APPS = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("POWOS_APPS_DIR", "~/.local/share/powos/apps"))
LIB = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
TEMPLATES = os.environ.get("POWOS_APP_TEMPLATES", os.path.join(LIB, "templates"))
# Where modules cross-compile (powos app builder): "user@host" (ssh), "local", or unset (here if the toolchain is).
BUILDER_CONF = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("POWOS_APP_BUILDER_CONF", "~/.config/powos/app-builder"))
# The cargo registry, the git checkouts and one shared target dir, on the builder: every app's dependencies (the
# spacetimedb crate and its ~90 others) compile once there, not once per app. apps/build.sh uses the same volume.
CACHE_VOLUME = "powos-apps-cargo"
BUILDER_IMAGE = "powos-app-builder"
LOCAL_TARGET = os.path.expanduser("~/.cache/powos/app-target")
# Parts of a template (lib/apps/templates/<part>/), copied in this order.
TEMPLATE_SETS = {
    "spacetimedb-astro": ["module", "ui", "page", "widget"],
    "widget": ["module", "ui", "widget"],
    "module-only": ["module"],
}
# What the shell's import map gives every page and widget (shell/index.html): one copy each for the whole shell.
UI_EXTERNALS = ["preact", "preact/hooks", "preact/jsx-runtime", "@preact/signals", "@preact/signals-core", "spacetimedb"]
APP_ID = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}$")


class Fail(Exception):
    pass


def die(msg):
    raise Fail(msg)


def log(msg):
    print(msg, flush=True)


def ms(t0):
    return int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)


def spacetime(*args, check=True, quiet=False):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["spacetime", *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die("no spacetime CLI here (PowOS ships it: the spacetimedb package)")
    out = "\n".join(line for line in (r.stdout + r.stderr).splitlines() if "UNSTABLE" not in line and line.strip())
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        die(f"spacetime {args[0]} failed:\n{out}")
    if not quiet and out:
        print(out)
    return r.returncode, out


def sql(db, query):
    code, out = spacetime("sql", "-s", SERVER, db, query, check=False, quiet=True)
    return code == 0, out


def ensure_registry():
    ok, _ = sql(REGISTRY, "SELECT id FROM app")
    if ok:
        return
    if not os.path.isfile(REGISTRY_WASM):
        die(f"no registry on {SERVER} and no {REGISTRY_WASM} to publish it from")
    print(f"publishing {REGISTRY} (the app registry; you are its owner)")
    spacetime("publish", "-y", "-s", SERVER, "--bin-path", REGISTRY_WASM, REGISTRY)


def manifest(d):
    p = os.path.join(d, "powos-app.json")
    try:
        with open(p) as f:
            text = f.read()
        return json.loads(text), text
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        die(f"{p}: {e}")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- new


def icon_svg(name, app_id):
    """A rounded square in a colour of its own (from the id) with the name's first letter: replace ui/icon.svg."""
    hue = int(hashlib.sha256(app_id.encode()).hexdigest()[:4], 16) % 360
    letter = (name.strip()[:1] or "?").upper().replace("&", "&amp;").replace("<", "&lt;")
    return (
        '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 96 96">'
        f'<rect width="96" height="96" rx="24" fill="hsl({hue} 55% 45%)"/>'
        '<text x="48" y="64" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="48" font-weight="600" fill="#fff" '
        f'text-anchor="middle">{letter}</text></svg>\n'
    )


def cmd_new(a):
    if not a or a[0].startswith("-"):
        die("usage: powos app new <name|id> [--name \"Shown name\"] [--template spacetimedb-astro|widget|module-only] [--dir D]")
    ident = a[0].lower()
    opts = flags(a[1:], {"--name": 1, "--template": 1, "--dir": 1})
    app_id = ident if "." in ident else f"local.{ident}"
    if not APP_ID.match(app_id) or ".." in app_id:
        die(f"bad id {app_id!r}: a-z 0-9 . - only, starting with a letter or digit")
    slug = app_id.rsplit(".", 1)[-1]
    if not slug:
        die(f"bad id {app_id!r}")
    template = opts.get("--template", "spacetimedb-astro")
    if template not in TEMPLATE_SETS:
        die(f"no template {template!r} ({', '.join(TEMPLATE_SETS)})")
    name = opts.get("--name") or slug.replace("-", " ").title()
    # It goes into TSX text and a Rust comment: nothing that would break either.
    name = re.sub(r"[{}<>`\\\"$]", "", name).strip() or slug
    d = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(opts.get("--dir") or os.path.join("~/Projects", slug)))
    # Dotfiles don't count (an agent's own state in its fresh working directory).
    if os.path.exists(d) and [x for x in os.listdir(d) if not x.startswith(".")]:
        die(f"{d} exists and isn't empty (--dir elsewhere)")
    db = app_id.replace(".", "-")
    crate = "powos-app-" + slug
    subst = {"__NAME__": name, "__ID__": app_id, "__DB__": db, "__CRATE__": crate}
    parts = TEMPLATE_SETS[template]
    for part in parts:
        src = os.path.join(TEMPLATES, part)
        if not os.path.isdir(src):
            die(f"{src} missing (the PowOS install's app templates)")
        for root, _, files in os.walk(src):
            for f in files:
                rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.join(root, f), src)
                with open(os.path.join(root, f)) as fh:
                    text = fh.read()
                for k, v in subst.items():
                    text = text.replace(k, v)
                out = os.path.join(d, rel)
                os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out), exist_ok=True)
                with open(out, "w") as fh:
                    fh.write(text)
    has_ui = "ui" in parts
    m = {
        "id": app_id,
        "name": name,
        "version": "0.1.0",
        "description": "",
        **({"icon": "icon.svg"} if has_ui else {}),
        "ui": {"dir": "out/ui/"} if has_ui else None,
        **({"page": {"entry": "pages/main.js"}} if "page" in parts else {}),
        "module": {"path": "module/", "lang": "rust", "database": db, "stdb": "2.12"},
        "backend": None,
        "widgets": [
            {"id": "main", "name": name, "kind": "island", "entry": "widgets/main.js", "size": "4x2", "minSize": "2x1"}
        ]
        if "widget" in parts
        else [],
        "surfaces": {"launcher": "page" in parts, "desktop": True},
        "permissions": [],
        "budget": {"phone": {"memMB": 16, "idle": "unload"}, "desktop": {"memMB": 32}},
    }
    with open(os.path.join(d, "powos-app.json"), "w") as f:
        json.dump(m, f, indent=2)
        f.write("\n")
    if has_ui:
        with open(os.path.join(d, "ui", "icon.svg"), "w") as f:
            f.write(icon_svg(name, app_id))
    with open(os.path.join(d, ".gitignore"), "w") as f:
        f.write("out/\nmodule/target/\nui/bindings/\n")
    log(f"made {app_id} ({name}, template {template}) in {d}")
    log(f"  database {db}; module/src/lib.rs" + (", ui/pages/main.tsx" if "page" in parts else "")
        + (", ui/widgets/main.tsx" if "widget" in parts else ""))
    log(f"next: powos app install {d}   then: powos app dev {d} (hot reload while you edit)")


def flags(a, spec):
    """--flag value pairs (spec: flag -> 1 takes a value, 0 doesn't); anything else is refused."""
    out, i = {}, 0
    while i < len(a):
        k = a[i]
        if k not in spec:
            die(f"unknown option {k} (powos app help)")
        if spec[k]:
            if i + 1 >= len(a):
                die(f"{k} needs a value")
            out[k] = a[i + 1]
            i += 2
        else:
            out[k] = True
            i += 1
    return out


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- build


def builder():
    v = os.environ.get("POWOS_APP_BUILDER")
    if v is None:
        try:
            with open(BUILDER_CONF) as f:
                v = f.read().strip()
        except OSError:
            v = ""
    return v or None


def cmd_builder(a):
    if not a:
        b = builder()
        log(b or f"not set: modules build here {'(cargo + wasm32 found)' if local_rust() else '- but there is no cargo + wasm32 here: set one'}")
        return
    v = a[0]
    if v not in ("local", "off") and not re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+@[A-Za-z0-9._:-]+$", v):
        die("powos app builder user@host | local | off")
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BUILDER_CONF), exist_ok=True)
    if v == "off":
        if os.path.exists(BUILDER_CONF):
            os.unlink(BUILDER_CONF)
        log("app builder: not set")
        return
    with open(BUILDER_CONF, "w") as f:
        f.write(v + "\n")
    if v != "local":
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        r = subprocess.run(ssh_cmd(v, "export PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:$PATH; docker version -f {{.Server.Version}} || cargo --version"),
                           capture_output=True, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            log(f"note: {v} didn't answer ({(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[:200]}); it's set anyway")
        else:
            log(f"app builder: {v} (docker {r.stdout.strip()}, {ms(t0)} ms round trip)")
            return
    log(f"app builder: {v}")


def ssh_cmd(target, command):
    return ["ssh", "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=5", "-o", "StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new",
            "-o", "ServerAliveInterval=15", target, command]


def local_rust():
    if not shutil.which("cargo") or not shutil.which("rustc"):
        return False
    r = subprocess.run(["rustc", "--print", "sysroot"], capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode == 0 and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(r.stdout.strip(), "lib", "rustlib", "wasm32-unknown-unknown"))


def tree_hash(d, skip=()):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    if not os.path.isdir(d):
        return "none"
    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(d):
        dirs[:] = sorted(x for x in dirs if os.path.relpath(os.path.join(root, x), d) not in skip)
        for f in sorted(files):
            p = os.path.join(root, f)
            rel = os.path.relpath(p, d)
            if rel in skip:
                continue
            h.update(rel.encode() + b"\0")
            with open(p, "rb") as fh:
                h.update(fh.read())
    return h.hexdigest()


def crate_name(mod_dir):
    with open(os.path.join(mod_dir, "Cargo.toml")) as f:
        m = re.search(r'^name\s*=\s*"([^"]+)"', f.read(), re.M)
    if not m:
        die(f"{mod_dir}/Cargo.toml: no package name")
    return m.group(1).replace("-", "_")


# Runs on the builder (bash, over ssh): the module's source comes in on stdin (a tar), the wasm goes out on stdout
# (a tar: module.wasm and the Cargo.lock cargo settled on), cargo's messages on stderr. In a container with the cargo
# cache volume - nothing of the app's is left on the builder - or with the builder's own cargo when it has no docker.
REMOTE_BUILD = r"""
set -e
export PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:$HOME/.cargo/bin:$PATH
if command -v docker >/dev/null 2>&1 && docker info >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null; then
  if ! docker image inspect "$IMAGE" >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null; then
    echo "builder: making the $IMAGE image (once: rust + the wasm32 target)" >&2
    printf 'FROM rust:1-bookworm\nRUN rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown\n' | docker build -q -t "$IMAGE" - >&2
  fi
  exec docker run --rm -i --cpus 6 --memory 8g -v "$VOLUME:/cache" -e CARGO_HOME=/cache/cargo -e CRATE "$IMAGE" bash -c "$INNER"
fi
command -v cargo >/dev/null || { echo "builder $(hostname): neither docker nor cargo" >&2; exit 3; }
CACHE=$HOME/.cache/powos-app-builder; mkdir -p "$CACHE"; export CACHE; exec bash -c "$INNER"
"""
REMOTE_INNER = r"""
set -e
W=$(mktemp -d); trap 'rm -rf $W' EXIT
tar -xz -C $W
T=${CACHE:-/cache}/target-powos-apps
cd $W/module
CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$T cargo build --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -q >&2
cp $T/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/$CRATE.wasm $W/module.wasm
tar -cz -C $W module.wasm module/Cargo.lock
"""


def build_module(d, m, where=None, force=False):
    """The module -> out/module.wasm, and its TS bindings -> ui/bindings. False when it was up to date."""
    mod = os.path.join(d, (m.get("module") or {}).get("path", "module/").rstrip("/"))
    if not m.get("module") or not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(mod, "Cargo.toml")):
        return False
    out = os.path.join(d, "out")
    os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)
    wasm = os.path.join(out, "module.wasm")
    stamp = os.path.join(out, ".module.sha")
    src = tree_hash(mod, skip={"target", "Cargo.lock"})
    try:
        with open(stamp) as f:
            same = f.read().strip() == src
    except OSError:
        same = False
    ui = os.path.join(d, "ui")
    if same and os.path.isfile(wasm) and not force:
        if os.path.isdir(ui) and not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(ui, "bindings")):
            bindings(d, wasm)
        return False
    crate = crate_name(mod)
    b = where or builder()
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    if b == "local" or (b is None and local_rust()):
        if not local_rust():
            die("no cargo + wasm32 target here (rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown), or: powos app builder user@host")
        r = subprocess.run(["cargo", "build", "--release", "--target", "wasm32-unknown-unknown", "-q"], cwd=mod,
                           env={**os.environ, "CARGO_TARGET_DIR": LOCAL_TARGET})
        if r.returncode != 0:
            die("module: cargo build failed")
        shutil.copy(os.path.join(LOCAL_TARGET, "wasm32-unknown-unknown", "release", crate + ".wasm"), wasm)
        how = "here"
    elif b is None:
        die("module: no Rust toolchain here and no app builder set - powos app builder user@host (a machine with "
            "docker), or install cargo + the wasm32 target")
    else:
        buf = io.BytesIO()
        with tarfile.open(fileobj=buf, mode="w:gz") as t:
            t.add(mod, arcname="module", filter=lambda ti: None if ti.name.startswith("module/target") else ti)
        env = " ".join(f"{k}={shlex.quote(v)}" for k, v in
                       {"IMAGE": BUILDER_IMAGE, "VOLUME": CACHE_VOLUME, "CRATE": crate, "INNER": REMOTE_INNER}.items())
        for attempt in range(3):
            r = subprocess.run(ssh_cmd(b, f"{env} bash -c {shlex.quote(REMOTE_BUILD)}"), input=buf.getvalue(),
                               stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
            # 255: ssh itself failed (no route yet after a wake, a refused login) - not the build: again, shortly.
            if r.returncode != 255:
                break
            time.sleep(1 + attempt)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            die(f"module: the build on {b} failed (exit {r.returncode})")
        with tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(r.stdout), mode="r:gz") as t:
            got = t.extractfile("module.wasm").read()
            lock = t.extractfile("module/Cargo.lock").read()
        with open(wasm + ".tmp", "wb") as f:
            f.write(got)
        os.replace(wasm + ".tmp", wasm)
        lp = os.path.join(mod, "Cargo.lock")
        if not os.path.isfile(lp) or open(lp, "rb").read() != lock:
            with open(lp, "wb") as f:
                f.write(lock)
        how = f"on {b}"
    with open(stamp, "w") as f:
        f.write(src + "\n")
    log(f"module: built {how} in {ms(t0)} ms ({os.path.getsize(wasm) // 1024} KB)")
    if os.path.isdir(ui):
        bindings(d, wasm)
    return True


def bindings(d, wasm):
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    out = os.path.join(d, "ui", "bindings")
    tmp = out + ".new"
    shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)
    spacetime("generate", "--lang", "typescript", "--out-dir", tmp, "--bin-path", wasm, "-y", quiet=True)
    shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)
    os.rename(tmp, out)
    log(f"bindings: ui/bindings in {ms(t0)} ms")


def build_ui(d, m):
    """ui/ -> out/ui: static files as they are, pages and widgets bundled one ES module each (the shell's own Preact
    and SpacetimeDB SDK stay imports), workers bundled whole (a worker has no import map)."""
    ui = os.path.join(d, "ui")
    if not m.get("ui") or not os.path.isdir(ui):
        return False
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    out = os.path.join(d, "out", "ui")
    new = os.path.join(d, "out", ".ui-new")
    shutil.rmtree(new, ignore_errors=True)
    os.makedirs(new)
    entries, workers = [], []
    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(ui):
        rel_root = os.path.relpath(root, ui)
        if rel_root == "bindings" or rel_root.startswith("bindings" + os.sep) or "node_modules" in rel_root:
            dirs[:] = []
            continue
        for f in files:
            rel = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel_root, f))
            top = rel.split(os.sep)[0]
            if f.endswith((".ts", ".tsx", ".jsx")) or f == "tsconfig.json":
                if top in ("pages", "widgets") and os.sep in rel and rel.count(os.sep) == 1 and not f.endswith(".d.ts"):
                    entries.append(rel)
                elif top == "workers" and rel.count(os.sep) == 1:
                    workers.append(rel)
                continue
            os.makedirs(os.path.join(new, os.path.dirname(rel)), exist_ok=True)
            shutil.copyfile(os.path.join(ui, rel), os.path.join(new, rel))
    schema = tree_hash(os.path.join(ui, "bindings"))[:16]
    if entries:
        bundle(ui, entries, new, externals=UI_EXTERNALS, define={"__POWOS_SCHEMA__": json.dumps(schema)})
    if workers:
        bundle(ui, workers, new, externals=[], define={})
    shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)
    os.rename(new, out)
    log(f"ui: {len(entries)} bundled{f' + {len(workers)} workers' if workers else ''} in {ms(t0)} ms")
    return True


def bundle(ui, entries, outdir, externals, define):
    if shutil.which("bun"):
        cmd = ["bun", "build", *entries, "--outdir", outdir, "--root", ".", "--format", "esm", "--target", "browser",
               "--minify"]
        for e in externals:
            cmd += ["--external", e]
        for k, v in define.items():
            cmd += ["--define", f"{k}={v}"]
    elif shutil.which("esbuild"):
        cmd = ["esbuild", *entries, "--bundle", "--format=esm", "--target=es2022", "--jsx=automatic",
               "--jsx-import-source=preact", "--minify", f"--outdir={outdir}", "--outbase=.", "--log-level=warning"]
        cmd += [f"--external:{e}" for e in externals] + [f"--define:{k}={v}" for k, v in define.items()]
    else:
        die("ui: no bun or esbuild here (PowOS ships bun)")
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=ui, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        die(f"ui: bundling failed:\n{(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()}")


def built(d, m):
    has_mod = m.get("module") and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, (m["module"].get("path") or "module/"), "Cargo.toml"))
    return (not has_mod or os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, "out", "module.wasm"))) and (
        not m.get("ui") or os.path.isdir(os.path.join(d, (m["ui"].get("dir") or "out/ui/").rstrip("/"))))


def cmd_build(d, a):
    opts = flags(a, {"--local": 0, "--remote": 0, "--module": 0, "--ui": 0, "--force": 0})
    m, _ = manifest(d)
    where = "local" if "--local" in opts else None
    if "--remote" in opts:
        where = builder()
        if not where or where == "local":
            die("--remote: no app builder set (powos app builder user@host)")
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    if "--ui" not in opts:
        if not build_module(d, m, where, force="--force" in opts) and m.get("module"):
            log("module: unchanged")
    if "--module" not in opts:
        build_ui(d, m)
    log(f"built {m['id']} in {ms(t0)} ms")


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ install


def live_schema(db):
    """The module live in [db] on this device, as its schema's fingerprint (spacetime describe); None: no such db."""
    code, out = spacetime("describe", "-s", SERVER, "--json", db, check=False, quiet=True)
    return hashlib.sha256(out.encode()).hexdigest() if code == 0 and out.strip() else None


def file_sha(p):
    with open(p, "rb") as f:
        return hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()


def publish_module(d, m):
    mod = m.get("module")
    if not mod:
        return
    wasm = os.path.join(d, "out", "module.wasm")
    if not os.path.isfile(wasm):
        die(f"{wasm} missing (powos app build {d})")
    # Published outside the ship service (apps/install.sh run by it sets POWOS_SHIPPED=1): said loudly - a schema
    # ahead of what other apps' bindings decode breaks their subscriptions (2026-10-30: powos-agents' work.try_line,
    # published from an agent's worktree before the shell's bindings had it).
    if not os.environ.get("POWOS_SHIPPED"):
        print(f"powos app: WARNING - publishing {mod['database']} outside the ship service: if its schema changed, "
              "every client's bindings must already have the change (tools/phone/ship.sh ships the module with them)",
              file=sys.stderr)
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    # Additive schema changes migrate in place; anything destructive is refused by the server (no --delete-data).
    spacetime("publish", "-y", "-s", SERVER, "--bin-path", wasm, mod["database"], quiet=True)
    # What's live now, to compare with next time (ensure_published).
    with open(os.path.join(d, "out", ".published"), "w") as f:
        json.dump({"database": mod["database"], "wasm": file_sha(wasm), "live": live_schema(mod["database"])}, f)
    log(f"module: published to {mod['database']} in {ms(t0)} ms (clients stay connected)")


def ensure_published(d, m):
    """Publishes the module unless the device already runs this very build: the wasm is the one last published from
    here AND the live module's schema is the one it had then. Not trusted: "the local build didn't change" - the
    database may run another module (an older publish from elsewhere, a reset), whatever this directory built."""
    mod = m.get("module")
    wasm = os.path.join(d, "out", "module.wasm")
    if not mod or not os.path.isfile(wasm):
        return publish_module(d, m)
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(d, "out", ".published")) as f:
            rec = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        rec = {}
    live = live_schema(mod["database"])
    if (live and rec.get("database") == mod["database"] and rec.get("wasm") == file_sha(wasm)
            and rec.get("live") == live):
        log(f"module: live in {mod['database']} is this build")
        return
    if live and rec.get("live") and rec.get("live") != live:
        log(f"module: {mod['database']} runs another module than this build's - publishing this one")
    publish_module(d, m)


def install_ui(d, m):
    """The UI installed atomically, every time: written whole into a new dir (<version>+<time>), then `current`
    flipped to it in one rename - the shell sees the old UI or the new one, never a half-copied one (a widget that
    loaded mid-copy 404'd and stayed broken). The previous one stays (rollback = flip back); older ones go.
    Returns how many files differ from the previous one."""
    src = os.path.join(d, (m.get("ui") or {}).get("dir", "ui").rstrip("/"))
    base = os.path.join(APPS, m["id"])
    os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)
    current = os.path.join(base, "current")
    previous = os.path.realpath(current) if os.path.lexists(current) else None
    name = f"{m['version']}+{int(time.time() * 1000)}"
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=base, prefix=".new-")
    # Plain writes, not copytree/copy2: those copy extended attributes too, security.selinux among them - the
    # source tree's label (system_data_root_file on the phone) landed on the installed dir and the PowOS app
    # (privapp_data_file only) could read none of it. New files get their dir's label.
    if os.path.isdir(src):
        sync(src, os.path.join(tmp, "ui"))
    sync_file(os.path.join(d, "powos-app.json"), os.path.join(tmp, "powos-app.json"))
    for root, dirs, _ in os.walk(tmp):
        for x in dirs:
            os.chmod(os.path.join(root, x), 0o755)
    os.chmod(tmp, 0o755)
    os.rename(tmp, os.path.join(base, name))
    link = os.path.join(base, ".current-new")
    if os.path.lexists(link):
        os.unlink(link)
    os.symlink(name, link)
    os.replace(link, current)  # atomic: the shell sees the old version or the new one
    changed = -1
    if previous and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(previous, "ui")):
        changed = sum(1 for _ in diff_files(os.path.join(previous, "ui"), os.path.join(base, name, "ui")))
    # Everything but this one and the previous one goes (half-made .new- dirs of a crashed install too).
    keep = {name, os.path.basename(previous) if previous else None}
    for v in os.listdir(base):
        if v == "current" or v in keep or v == ".current-new":
            continue
        shutil.rmtree(os.path.join(base, v), ignore_errors=True)
    if not mounted(APPS) and os.path.exists("/run/powos-app"):
        print(f"note: {APPS} isn't the PowOS app's files/apps here (start a new session): the shell won't see it")
    return changed


def diff_files(a, b):
    """Paths that differ between two trees (added, removed or changed)."""
    def files(r):
        out = {}
        for root, _, fs in os.walk(r):
            for f in fs:
                p = os.path.join(root, f)
                out[os.path.relpath(p, r)] = p
        return out
    fa, fb = files(a), files(b)
    for rel in set(fa) | set(fb):
        if rel not in fa or rel not in fb:
            yield rel
            continue
        with open(fa[rel], "rb") as x, open(fb[rel], "rb") as y:
            if x.read() != y.read():
                yield rel


def sync_file(a, b):
    try:
        with open(a, "rb") as f:
            new = f.read()
    except OSError:
        return 0
    try:
        with open(b, "rb") as f:
            if f.read() == new:
                return 0
    except OSError:
        pass
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(b), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(b), "." + os.path.basename(b) + ".new")
    with open(tmp, "wb") as f:
        f.write(new)
    os.chmod(tmp, 0o644)
    os.replace(tmp, b)
    return 1


def sync(src, dest):
    """dest becomes src: changed files replaced, new ones added, gone ones removed. How many changed."""
    n = 0
    want = set()
    for root, _, files in os.walk(src):
        for f in files:
            rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.join(root, f), src)
            want.add(rel)
            n += sync_file(os.path.join(src, rel), os.path.join(dest, rel))
    for root, _, files in os.walk(dest):
        for f in files:
            rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.join(root, f), dest)
            if rel not in want:
                os.unlink(os.path.join(dest, rel))
                n += 1
    return n


def mounted(path):
    """A mount point, binds of the same filesystem included (os.path.ismount only sees a device change)."""
    try:
        with open("/proc/self/mountinfo") as f:
            return any(line.split()[4] == os.path.realpath(path) for line in f)
    except OSError:
        return os.path.ismount(path)


def register(text):
    spacetime("call", "-s", SERVER, REGISTRY, "install", json.dumps(text), quiet=True)


def units():
    from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
    from importlib.util import module_from_spec, spec_from_loader
    p = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "powos-units")
    if not os.path.exists(p):
        return None
    loader = SourceFileLoader("powos_units", p)
    mod = module_from_spec(spec_from_loader("powos_units", loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def register_unit(m):
    """The installed app as a unit (lib/apps/powos-units): its files, its backend's process and limits, its owner,
    how it goes (powos app remove). An app's dependencies live in its module or its container, never on the host."""
    u = units()
    if u is None:
        return
    b = m.get("backend") or {}
    unit = {"id": m["id"], "name": m.get("name", m["id"]), "kind": "app", "owner": u.owner_default(),
            "purpose": (m.get("description") or f"the PowOS app {m.get('name', m['id'])}")[:300],
            "installedBy": "powos app install", "files": [os.path.join(APPS, m["id"])],
            "database": (m.get("module") or {}).get("database", ""),
            "remove": {"commands": [f"powos app remove {m['id']}"]}}
    if b.get("exec"):
        unit["processes"] = [{"match": re.escape(b["exec"][0])}]
        budget = (m.get("budget") or {})
        bud = budget.get(u.HOST if u.HOST in budget else "phone" if u.HOST.startswith("phone") else "desktop") or {}
        if bud.get("memMB"):
            unit["limits"] = {"memory": f"{int(bud['memMB']) * 2}m", "pids": int(bud.get("pids", 512))}
    if m.get("autosleep") is not None:
        unit["autosleep"] = m["autosleep"]
    try:
        u.register(unit, quiet=True)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        log(f"note: not registered as a unit ({e})")


def cmd_install(d):
    m, text = manifest(d)
    # Always: an unchanged module isn't rebuilt (its source hash), and the UI bundles in ~0.1 s - an install never
    # ships a UI older than its source (it did: ui/lib edited, out/ui kept).
    cmd_build(d, [])
    ensure_registry()
    ensure_published(d, m)
    install_ui(d, m)
    register(text)
    register_unit(m)
    page = (m.get("page") or {}).get("entry")
    log(f"installed {m['id']} {m['version']}" + (" - in the drawer" if page else "")
        + (f", {len(m.get('widgets') or [])} widget(s) in home's edit sheet" if m.get("widgets") else ""))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- dev


def scan(d):
    """Every source file's (mtime, size): what `dev` compares. Not the build's own output."""
    skip = {"out", ".git", "node_modules", os.path.join("module", "target"), os.path.join("ui", "bindings")}
    seen = {}
    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(d):
        rel_root = os.path.relpath(root, d)
        dirs[:] = [x for x in dirs if os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel_root, x)) not in skip]
        for f in files:
            rel = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel_root, f))
            if rel == os.path.join("module", "Cargo.lock") or f.endswith(("~", ".swp")) or f.startswith(".#"):
                continue
            try:
                st = os.stat(os.path.join(root, f))
            except OSError:
                continue
            seen[rel] = (st.st_mtime_ns, st.st_size)
    return seen


def cmd_dev(d):
    d = os.path.abspath(d)
    m, text = manifest(d)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(APPS, m["id"], "current")):
        cmd_install(d)
    else:
        build_module(d, m)
        ensure_published(d, m)
        build_ui(d, m)
        install_ui(d, m)
    log(f"dev: watching {d} - save a file and it's live (Ctrl-C stops)")
    snap = scan(d)
    while True:
        # HACK: polls (a stat of each source file, 4x a second, only while `dev` runs): Python has no inotify in its
        # standard library. Real fix: inotify through ctypes (or inotifywait when the image ships inotify-tools).
        time.sleep(0.25)
        now = scan(d)
        if now == snap:
            continue
        # An editor's save can be several writes: once it has settled.
        time.sleep(0.05)
        now = scan(d)
        changed = sorted(k for k in set(snap) | set(now) if snap.get(k) != now.get(k))
        snap = now
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        try:
            if "powos-app.json" in changed:
                m, text = manifest(d)
            if any(c.startswith("module" + os.sep) for c in changed):
                if build_module(d, m):
                    publish_module(d, m)
            if build_ui(d, m):
                install_ui(d, m)
            if "powos-app.json" in changed:
                register(text)
            log(f"live in {ms(t0)} ms: {', '.join(changed)[:120]}")
        except Fail as e:
            log(f"error: {e}")
        snap = scan(d)


